in series produces visible muscle contraction\n\n**Significance:**\nThe constant A band length during contraction demonstrates that muscle shortening occurs through filament sliding rather than filament shortening, confirming the sliding filament theory proposed by Huxley and Hanson. The force generated depends on the degree of overlap between thick and thin filaments, explaining the length-tension relationship in muscle physiology."
